  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 10\nDEMS-RSMC SPECIAL TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 02.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 10 FOR NORTH INDIAN OCEAN (THE BAY OF\nBENGAL AND ARABIAN SEA) ISSUED AT 1500 UTC OF 02.11.2026 BASED ON 1200 UTC\nOF 02.11.2026\nSub: - Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] over Westcentral Bay of Bengal\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over Westcentral Bay of Bengal moved\nnorth-northwestwards with a speed of 12 kmph during past 06 hours and lay centered at 1200 UTC of\ntoday, the 02nd November, 2026 over the same region near Latitude 14.7\u00b0N and Longitude 80.7\u00b0E, about\n80 km east-northeast of Nellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh), 80 km east-southeast of Kavali (43243, Andhra\nPradesh), 110 km southeast of Ongole (43221, Andhra Pradesh), 190 km north-northeast of Chennai\n(Tamil Nadu) and 170 km south-southwest of Machilipatnam (43185, Andhra Pradesh).\nIt is very likely to move northwestwards and cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a Severe Cyclonic Storm\nwith wind speed of 100 to 110 kmph gusting to 120 kmph between Nellore(Andhra Pradesh, 43245) and\nNarsapur (Andhra Pradesh, 43187) close to Ongole(Andhra Pradesh, 43221) during 1800-2200 UTC of\n2nd November, 2026.\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather\nRadars at Chennai, Machilipatnam and Visakhapatnam.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak: Cloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-\n25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very Intense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of\ndepression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-66% and HIGH:67-100%\nThis is a guidance Bulletin for WMO/ESCAP Panel Member countries. Visit respective National websites for Country specific Bulletins.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n02.11.26/1200 14.7/80.7 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n02.11.26/1800 15.1/80.3 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0000 15.6/80.0 90-100 gusting to 110 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0600 15.9/79.8 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1200 16.3/79.6 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n04.11.26/0000 17.1/79.4 50-60 gusting to 70 Deep Depression\n04.11.26/1200 14.7/80.7 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\nThe estimated central pressure is 994.0 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 55 kt\ngusting to 65kt.\nNellore reported mean sea level (MSLP) of 1007.8 hPa, 24 hours pressure change (P24) as -2.9\nhPa and maximum sustained wind speed (MSW) as 2900/08kt, Kavali reported MSLP of 1008.0\nhPa, P24 as -3.4 hPa and MSW 3400/09kt, Bapatla reported MSLP of 1009.9 hPa, P24 as -1.1\nhPa and MSW 3600/10kt, Ongole reported MSLP of 1008.9 hPa, P24 as -1.6 hPa and MSW\n0500/04kt.\nAs per latest INSAT 3DS imagery based on 1200 UTC, intensity of the system is T3.5. Irregular\nCDO pattern is seen. Centre is embedded in CDO. Associated scattered to broken low and\nmedium clouds with embedded intense to very intense convection lay over west Bay of Bengal\n(minimum CTT is",
